    "answer": {
      "short": "Only common factors of the entire numerator and denominator can be cancelled, not individual terms. For $x=2$, $\\frac{x+3}{x+5}=\\frac{5}{7}\\ne\\frac{3}{5}$.",
      "worked": "Only common factors of the entire numerator and denominator can be cancelled, not individual terms. Here, $x$ is not a factor of either entire expression.\n\nFor $x=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x+3}{x+5}&=\\frac{2+3}{2+5}\\\\&=\\frac{5}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac{5}{7}\\ne\\frac{3}{5}$, this is a numerical counterexample.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
